# b00t Assimilate Schema datum
# .tomllmd — mdtable format for column-stable serialization
# schema: 1 | bump ONLY on field definition changes
# last_updated: 2026-05-04
#
# 🤓 The Assimilate pipeline provides indelible document-level attribution for
#    grok knowledge. Every knowledge chunk traces back to its source document
#    via content-addressed DocumentId and position-stamped chunk containers.
#    A transaction log (append-only JSONL) enables replay to rebuild the
#    knowledgebase from scratch after corruption.
#
# 🔗参 b00t-c0re-lib/src/assimilate.rs — core types (DocumentRecord, ChunkRecord, TransactionLog)
# 🔗参 b00t-cli/src/commands/grok.rs — `b00t grok assimilate` CLI command
# 🔗参 vendor/l3dg3rr/crates/ledgerr-focus/ — FOCUS chunking (future: ledgrrr chunker)
# 🔗参 _b00t_/transactions/ — stored transaction logs (append-only JSONL)

[b00t]
name = "ASSIMILATE-SCHEMA"
type = "schema"
hint = "Assimilate pipeline schema — document ingestion, chunk attribution, transaction log, replay protocol for indelible grok knowledge"

[b00t.version]
schema = 1
content = "stable"

## Assimilate Pipeline Phases
## schema_version=1: these 4 columns in this order.

| phase | description | output |
|-------|-------------|--------|
| fetch | Download document from URL or read local file | raw bytes |
| hash | Compute blake3 content hash → DocumentId | doc_id (hex) |
| chunk | Split document into position-stamped chunks via ledgrrr | Vec<ChunkRecord> |
| wrap | Wrap each chunk in <container> span with doc_id, chunk_id, pos, sig | Vec<String> container spans |
| store | Write transaction(s) to log + persist to irontology | tx_log entry |

## DocumentRecord — source attribution for ingested documents
## schema_version=1: these 7 fields in this order.

| field | type | description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| doc_id | string | Content-addressed ID = blake3(content) hex |
| source_url | string? | URL where document was fetched (None for local files) |
| source_path | string? | Local file path (None for URLs) |
| title | string? | Document title (auto-detected or user-provided) |
| content_length | u64 | Size of original content in bytes |
| ingested_at | string | ISO 8601 timestamp of ingestion |
| content_hash | string | blake3 hash of normalized content (same as doc_id) |

## ChunkRecord — position-attested chunk with container span
## schema_version=1: these 7 fields in this order.

| field | type | description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| chunk_id | string | Qualified ID: `{doc_id}::chunk::{N}` |
| doc_id | string | Parent document ID |
| position | u32 | 0-indexed position within document |
| total_chunks | u32 | Total number of chunks for this document |
| container | string | Container span tag: `<container doc="{doc_id}" chunk="{chunk_id}" pos="{N}/{T}" sig="{content_hash}">` |
| content | string | The chunk text content |
| content_hash | string | blake3 hash of this chunk's content |

## Container Span Format
## schema_version=1: these 5 attributes on the <container> tag.

The container span wraps each chunk to maintain attribution through processing:

```
<container doc="<doc_id>" chunk="<chunk_id>" pos="<N>/<T>" sig="<content_hash>">
  ...chunk text content...
</container>
```

Where:
- `doc` — content-addressed DocumentId (blake3 of full document)
- `chunk` — qualified chunk ID: doc_id::chunk::N
- `pos` — position within document: "N/T" where N=0-indexed, T=total
- `sig` — blake3 hash of this chunk's content (inner integrity check)

## Transaction Log Entry
## schema_version=1: these 6+ fields in this order.
## Append-only JSONL at ~/.b00t/transactions/YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl

| field | type | description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| tx_id | string | Transaction ID = `{date}::{seq}` where seq is auto-incrementing per day |
| action | string | One of: ingest_doc, chunk, learn, verify |
| doc_id | string | Document ID being acted upon |
| chunk_id | string? | Chunk ID if action=chunk |
| timestamp | string | ISO 8601 timestamp |
| payload_hash | string | blake3 hash of the full transaction payload |

## Replay Protocol
## schema_version=1: these 4 columns in this order.

| step | action | description |
|------|--------|-------------|
| 1 | scan | Read all .jsonl files from ~/.b00t/transactions/ sorted by date |
| 2 | dedup | Skip duplicate tx_ids by checking payload_hash |
| 3 | re-assimilate | For each unique transaction, re-process: ingest_doc → re-chunk → re-store |
| 4 | verify | Compare chunk content_hash against stored hash — detect corruption |

